We are in method removeLastOccurrence(Object o) which returns boolean. The comment says: If the list originally contained the element 'o', then the result of the operation is true.

Thus specification: (\old(this.contains(o))) => \result == true. But more precisely, result is true if originally contained element. So assert: \old(this.contains(o)) => \result; Since \result is boolean, we can just use \result. Or equivalently \old(this.contains(o)) => \result == true.

Also maybe need to consider that if not contained, result could be false, but not required. So just assert the implication.

